 ## Overview
-The Scene Auto-Encoder is a method that encodes a set of RGB images with known camera poses and depth measurements into a 3D neural field represented as density and feature voxel grids, enabling novel view synthesis and serving as input for latent compression [S1]. It differs from its siblings, such as [Scene NeRF](12484-scene-nerf.md) and [NeRF-OSR](14477-nerf-osr.md), by explicitly constructing a discrete voxel-based representation via a 2D CNN encoder and frustum lifting, rather than relying solely on a continuous MLP to map coordinates to radiance [S1].
